  "title": "Chien-Shiung Wu",
  "summary": "Chien-Shiung Wu, a physicist born in 1912 near Shanghai, worked at Columbia University in New York. In 1956–57 her cobalt-60 beta-decay experiment, testing a proposal by Lee and Yang, showed that parity is not conserved in weak interactions. Lee and Yang received the 1957 Nobel Prize; she did not. She died in New York in 1997.",
